7558	    /// the next poll asks `finalize` again if it finishes. A refusal
7559	    /// pops the revision (in `apply_reply`) and the file goes with it,
7560	    /// so the next poll asks afresh. A lost reply keeps both: the round
7561	    /// may have started, and recovery asks about the send. The port's
7562	    /// `NO_ANSWER` is a lost reply too, since the app still has the
7563	    /// request. A revision of a round whose earlier send never opened it
7564	    /// is replaced, so each round has one, naming who answered last.
